done_when: |
  1. Live fetcher writes ONLY to data/{market}/live/{TOKEN}.parquet (never touches 1h_cache)
  2. build_parquet_cache writes ONLY to data/{market}/1h_cache/ (never touches live)
  3. A single load_token_data() function merges historical + live at read time
  4. All consumers (signals.py, portfolio_signals.py, paper_engine.py) use load_token_data()
  5. No two processes ever write to the same file
  6. All existing tests pass
  7. Paper trader works correctly with new data path

kill_criteria: |
  1. Separation adds >500ms latency to paper trader tick cycle
  2. Read-time merge produces different results than current approach
  3. Migration breaks >5% of existing tests
  4. Complexity exceeds benefit (if the fix is worse than the problem)

