notes: |
  === ARCHITECTURE ===

  AFTER migration:

  Layer 1: LIVE BUFFER (mutable, ephemeral)
    Location: data/{market}/live/{TOKEN}.parquet
    Writer:   live_fetcher.py (ONLY writer)
    Contains: bars newer than last historical bar
    Lifetime: until promoted to historical

  Layer 2: HISTORICAL STORE (immutable, append-only)
    Location: data/{market}/1h_cache/{TOKEN}_1h.parquet (existing)
    Writer:   build_parquet_cache.py for initial load, promote_live.py for ongoing
    Rule:     once written, NEVER modified by live_fetcher

  Layer 3: READ-TIME MERGE (virtual, no files)
    Function: v4/data_loader.py:load_token_data(token, market) → pd.DataFrame
    Used by:  signals.py, portfolio_signals.py, paper_engine.py
    Guarantees: deduped, sorted, type-consistent DatetimeIndex

  === KEY DESIGN DECISIONS ===

  D1. Parquet format preserved — no schema changes, no new dependencies
  D2. Historical files unchanged — build_parquet_cache.py continues to own them
  D3. Live buffer is small (hours to days of data) — fast reads
  D4. Read-time merge is cheap (concat + dedup + sort on small live buffer)
  D5. Backward compatible — if live/ doesn't exist, just read historical
